   "notes": [
    "Figures hold for factory test, where self-heating is negligible and TJ equals TA; with internal self-heating (TJ above TA) they are not guaranteed.",
    "Register values carry a b prefix for binary and 0x for hexadecimal; plain numbers are decimal.",
    "Min and max are guaranteed at 30 °C by test, design or statistics; across temperature they rest on statistical quality control correlation.",
    "Typical values are the most likely figure at characterization, untested and not guaranteed.",
    "Supply-current rows leave out I2C traffic and the current drawn through the SCL and SDA pull-ups.",
    "Average rows give the mean current while the conversion runs.",
    "Heater current, RH repeatability, RH conversion time and all three temperature rows are set by design or characterization, without production test.",
    "Hysteresis: the gap between readings at one RH point when approached from rising and from falling humidity.",
    "Response time depends on the thermal mass of the system and on air flow; t63% is the time for the output to cover 63 % of a step in humidity.",
    "The recommended RH range is 10 % to 70 %; long operation outside it can leave a reading offset, which shrinks once the sensor is back inside that range.",
    "Drift is from ageing at 30 °C and 20 % to 50 % RH; dust, solvent vapour, outgassing tapes, adhesives and packaging materials can change it."
