  {
   "id": "hvac-thermostat",
   "title": "Battery-powered HVAC thermostat",
   "page": 17,
   "description": "A lithium-ion cell powers a TPL5110 timer, which switches a P-channel MOSFET to feed the sensor, the microcontroller and the display from the cell. A push button runs from the cell to the timer's DELAY/M_DRIVE pin, which has a resistor to ground. The controller reads the sensor over I2C (pull-ups to the switched rail), signals DONE back to the timer from a GPIO, drives the display and reads the keypad from GPIOs, and has one GPIO out to the air-conditioning system.",
   "parts": [
